  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Money on a card, under a violet sky",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"Money on a card, under a violet sky\"**\n\nEvery screen is built from two layers. Above, a violet gradient band (the sky) carries the header, the page title and white chrome. Below, calm lavender ground. Between them, white cards with soft violet-tinted lift hold the money: the balance, the confirm rows, the result. The card overlaps the band, so the eye lands on it first. The grammar is the Copilot money app's (dashboard, sheet, keypad), rebuilt in Wallet's own purple; it replaced the black-and-white \"Clear Ledger\" world.\n\nThe mood is calm and soft, never loud. Density is moderate: one card per idea, generous section gaps, 64px list rows, 48px controls. Colour is rationed. Violet means you can act, it is selected, or it is the sky; green, amber and red appear only to state where money is.\n\nThe layout has two shapes from one system. On the web (1024px and up) a lavender sidebar sits beside a content column whose top carries the sky band. On the app (below 1024px) a transparent header floats over the sky with a centred title, and a white tab bar sits at the bottom with a raised violet Scan disc.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Lifted white cards over a violet sky band that fades into lavender ground.",
      "One violet: action, selection, focus, the sky, and the balance line.",
      "Status colour only for transaction states, rings and bars.",
      "The đồng sign set small and raised beside the numerals.",
      "Uppercase muted section labels with a quiet \"Xem tất cả ›\".",
      "A violet keypad panel with lavender keys for every amount entry.",
      "Every transaction outcome reads as one plain truth line."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Violet Rule",
        "body": "Violet is action, selection, focus, the sky, or the balance line. It never fills a status, a chart of limits, or a decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Status Is Truth Rule",
